<urn:atm:triage:finding/CPR-012>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "CPR-012" ;
  triage:title "Four BA.5 doc-named tests cannot fail" ;
  triage:description "Hostile closure review (general-purpose opus, task af4edaf6699568f49) @ 9f5aef2fe. Four BA.5 doc-named tests cannot fail. Doc says: sprint-BA.5 AC2: every named test exists and proves its line. Code does: restart_after_claim_reexposes_unread_item overwrites the claim lease with set_marker before observing it, so it passes identically against develop (i.e. it does not test the BA.5 change at all). ack_clears_marker_via_existing_upsert never acknowledges anything. immediate_send_never_carries_marker is vacuous — the fixture never produces a marker regardless. bare_cli_pull_closes_item asserts the opposite of its doc line. Recommendation: Rewrite all four against the property named in the doc. The genuine R3 boundary test in this suite is immediate_send_is_never_reminded — use it as the model. solar review-3 item B3, with negation proof per test." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-coverage" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/tests/herdr_nudge_invariant.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix (ATM 01M2A821M48VWSZ0JGXMA4WWZ7, 2026-09-12T07:24:38Z): fixed by solar review-3 at 2b599f12c. Sha remap (fenix ATM 01M2A9NY2AEAKS6EAHY0V4ZDYB, 2026-09-12T07:52:59Z): review-3 rebased onto review-2 33754d69d (force-with-lease); 2b599f12c -> c59d7c93b." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA6 ;
